  "wikitext": "{{Named item|Jewelry\n  | name                     = Kormor's Ring\n  | type                     = Ring\n  | class                    = Jewelry\n  | slot                     = Finger\n  | durability               = 120\n  | material                 = Gold\n  | hardness                 = 12\n  | basevalue                = 10,020 pp\n  | weight                   = 0.10 lbs\n  | minlevel                 = 18\n  | bind                     = {{Bind|BtC|BoA|1}}\n  | quest                    = Tower of Despair\n  | chest                    = right side end chest\n  | mythic                   = no\n  | enhancements             = \n* {{Stat|INT|6}}\n* {{Confounding Enchantment}} \n** ''Every time this ring is equipped, it gains one of the following until unequipped:''\n*** {{Stat|CHA|1|Exceptional}}\n*** {{Stat|CON|1|Exceptional}}\n*** {{Stat|DEX|1|Exceptional}}\n*** {{Stat|INT|1|Exceptional}}\n*** {{Stat|STR|1|Exceptional}}\n*** {{Stat|WIS|1|Exceptional}}\n* {{Named item sets|Wild Mage}}\n* {{CraftingEffects|Incredible Potential}}\n  | crafting                 = Incredible Potential\n  | craftingupgrade          = <!-- -->\n  | description              = This ring, once owned by the Wild Mage Kormor, is made of a strange material that vibrates with wild magic. The very enchantments on the ring seem to change while it is worn.\n  | tips                     = Confounding Enchantment provides a +1 exceptional bonus to a random ability. You'll get a new one every time you equip it, so you may un-equip and re-equip it until you get the +1 stat of your choice.\n  | pic                      = Ring Generic Gold.png\n  | picdesc                  = Kormor's Ring.png\n}}",
